**Yes—there is a plausible short paper here, centered on a precise conjecture equivalent to RH.** I created **“Finite response matrices for Weil positivity”** in the new folder directly under `papers`, using commit `efb908a`.

At a high level, the strongest arithmetic result isolates all possible negativity in a finite matrix for each interval. The latest manuscript supplies explicit boundary corrections and rigorous approximation bounds for that matrix. The supersymmetric constructions provide motivation, but the condensed argument does not require their more difficult physical identifications.

The proposed conjecture is

\[
\boxed{S_n=A_n-B_n^*H_n^{-1}B_n\succeq0
\quad\text{for every integer }n\ge1.}
\]

Here \(A_n\) describes the low modes, \(H_n\) the high modes—whose positivity is established unconditionally—and \(B_n\) their coupling. The conjecture says that the high-mode response never removes more energy than the low modes possess. The draft supplies both directions of the RH equivalence for your review, leaving this universal inequality conjectural.

The matrices are finite, although their entries involve an infinite-dimensional inverse controlled by the remainder estimates.

